  "body": "It's sad when people do `writer.abort()` with no arguments, because then the various promises (e.g., on any `writer.write()` calls, or `writer.closed`) reject with `undefined`.\r\n\r\nCould we instead automatically generate an `\"AbortError\"` `DOMException`? That would match the behavior of `AbortController`.",
